# Brand asset source library (large; processed output in public/brand is committed)
frontend/brand-src/*
# ...except Axcion's OWN identity, which is the product's rather than a customer's: 1.3MB of
# delivered masters that scripts/brand_assets.py regenerates every web asset from. Without them
# a checkout cannot rebuild the brand, and the test holding the committed assets to the delivery
# finds nothing to compare and passes -- a guard that silently checks nothing.
# The glob above is `/*` rather than `/` so git descends far enough to see this negation at all.
!frontend/brand-src/axcion/
LAUNCH-TAB-UI-BRIEF.md
backend/probe_bc_utm.py

# Recall.ai bot ledger (local, per-machine)
backend/scripts/.recall_bots.json
# Booking exports contain client names/emails — never commit
backend/scripts/*.csv

# COA discovery output — per-entity account names and balances, never commit
backend/coa_discovery_out/
backend/coa_report.txt
# The mapping worksheet carries real account names, including people's. Generated on
# demand by coa_worksheet.py; never a repo artefact.
backend/coa-mapping-worksheet.xlsx
backend/coa-mapping-worksheet*.xlsx
expense-normalization-2026-08/1 - Vendor Master.xlsx
expense-normalization-2026-08/2 - Entity Expense Summary.xlsx
expense-normalization-2026-08/3 - Shared Cost Candidates.xlsx
expense-normalization-2026-08/4 - Findings Memo.md

